Wed May 10 13:21:34 1995  John Salmon  <johns@mullet.anu.edu.au>

	* integrate_vrtx_helic.c (Update): Removed the code that
	puts "dead" vortices on a ring.  Just leave them where they
	are sitting in the input data.  This speeds things up A LOT
	because it eliminates thousands of trig function calls.

	* quads_vrtx.c (InteractCell): Test for dist==0, which can
	happen (rarely) if zero-strength vortices are present.

	* cofm_vrtx.c (CofmFromDaugh): Added a couple of extra tests
	to guard against div-by-zero and similar problems when dealing
	with zero-strength vortices.

